.TH YTSTREAM "1" "December 2025" "ytstream 202606040928-git" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytstream \- Open YouTube video in media player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytstream
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,URL|ID\/\fR [\fI\,URL|ID\/\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytstream
is a script for streaming YouTube videos directly in a media player without downloading. It extracts the video stream URL and opens it in the configured media player.
.PP
The script is useful for watching videos without storing them locally.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display help message with usage information and available options
.TP
.BR \-\-config
Generate or regenerate user configuration file with default settings
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show script version information and exit
.TP
.BR \-\-options
Display all available command-line options
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug mode with verbose output and command tracing (set -x)
.TP
.BR \-\-no-color
Disable colorized output for plain text display
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YTSTREAM_DEFAULT_PLAYER
Media player to use (default: the first of mpv, vlc, mplayer and cvlc that is installed). Set it in settings.conf, which takes precedence over the environment
.TP
.B YTSTREAM_DEFAULT_PLAYER_OPTIONS
Extra options passed to the player
.TP
.B YTSTREAM_DEFAULT_PLAYER_FORMAT
yt-dlp format selector (default: bestvideo*+bestaudio/best for mpv, best for other players)
.TP
.B YTSTREAM_COOKIE_FILE
Netscape-format cookies file passed to yt-dlp (default: ~/.config/myscripts/ytstream/cookies.txt)
.TP
.B YTSTREAM_JS_RUNTIME
JavaScript runtime for YouTube (deno, node, bun or quickjs). Detected automatically when unset; yt-dlp only enables deno on its own
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ytstream https://youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID
Stream YouTube video in media player
.TP
.B ytstream "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID"
Stream using short URL
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytstream/settings.conf
User configuration file for ytstream preferences
.TP
.B ~/.config/myscripts/ytstream/cookies.txt
Optional cookies file for videos that need a signed-in session
.TP
.B ~/.local/log/ytstream/play.log
Player and yt-dlp errors
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
No URL was given or no media player was found
.TP
.B 69
The stream for a URL could not be resolved (EX_UNAVAILABLE)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Streams without downloading
.IP \(bu 2
mpv is given the page URL and resolves it itself through yt-dlp, with the same JavaScript runtime and cookies. Other players get a direct stream URL from yt-dlp, and URLs are resolved before playback starts so errors show right away
.IP \(bu 2
If yt-dlp is missing it is installed with setupmgr
.IP \(bu 2
Requires internet connection
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
mpv/vlc - Media player with streaming support
.IP \(bu 2
yt-dlp - For URL extraction (installed with setupmgr when missing)
.RE
